18. Your existing PATCH has one important problem
You currently have:

Field actualFieldName =
        Employee.class.getDeclaredField(filedName);

actualFieldName.setAccessible(true);

actualFieldName.set(oldData, value);
This worked for:

{
    "empName": "Nandhini"
}
because empName is a String.

But now if you send:

{
    "dob": "1987-10-04"
}
Jackson gives your Map<String,Object> a value that is essentially a String, while your Employee field is:

LocalDate
Then reflection can fail because you're trying to put a String into a LocalDate.

Better version
Use Jackson's ObjectMapper.

Add:

@Autowired
private ObjectMapper objectMapper;
Import:

import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
Then:

@Override
public EmployeeDto updateEmp(
        int empid,
        Map<String, Object> updates)
        throws Exception {

    Employee oldData =
            employeeRepository.findById(empid)
            .orElseThrow(
                () -> new Exception("Emp ID not found")
            );


    for (Map.Entry<String, Object> entry
            : updates.entrySet()) {

        String fieldName = entry.getKey();

        Object value = entry.getValue();


        Field actualFieldName =
                Employee.class.getDeclaredField(fieldName);

        actualFieldName.setAccessible(true);


        Object convertedValue =
                objectMapper.convertValue(
                    value,
                    actualFieldName.getType()
                );


        actualFieldName.set(
                oldData,
                convertedValue
        );
    }


    Employee result =
            employeeRepository.save(oldData);

    return empToDto(result);
}
Now this works:

{
    "dob": "1990-05-15"
}
and:

{
    "doj": "2022-07-10"
}
